  "series": "Unity in Diversity",
  "comments": "Variants regarding the different form of the year see<br />\r\n<a href=\"http://monnaiesetvarietes.esy.es/FICHES/Inde/INDE%202%20Rupees%20KM%20326.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://monnaiesetvarietes.esy.es/FICHES/Inde/INDE%202%20Rupees%20KM%20326.pdf</a><br /><br />\r\n2005 Calcutta has two varieties - large and small date. There is not an obvious difference in the size of the text however the number 5 in the date shows a difference in thickness and design.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/62037ba5b895b.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/62037ba5b895b.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"75\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nIn 2006, some coins from Mumbai were struck with obverse die <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">3</span>: the top of &quot;6&quot; is wide and the bottom is narrow.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/58b20257392a0.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/58b20257392a0.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"146\" /></a><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5a96dea879e45.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5a96dea879e45.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nThere are two variants of the cross design.<br />\r\nSmall design: right vertical crossbar extends to the first E in RUPEES<br />\r\nLarge design: right vertical crossbar extends to the second E in RUPEES",
